# Route Integrity Guardrail

Do not remove, rename, repoint, or silently change behavior of existing routes unless the user explicitly asks for that specific route change.

## Required behavior before route edits

- Treat route behavior as backward-compatibility sensitive.
- If a change could affect existing paths, preserve old paths with compatibility handling whenever possible.
- If route removal is requested, confirm exactly which paths are affected and what replacement behavior is expected.

## What counts as route changes

- Entry/surface resolution logic (`src/main.tsx`, hostname/path routing, redirects)
- Navigation paths and deep links
- Route constants, helpers, rewrite/redirect config

## Safe default pattern

```ts
// ✅ Keep legacy path behavior while adding new behavior
if (path === '/order-manager') return renderOrderManagerApp();
if (path === '/order') return renderOrderApp();
```

```ts
// ❌ Do not collapse staff/public routes without explicit request
if (hostSurface === 'order') return renderOrderApp();
```
